menu "Host power save example"

    config APP_WIFI_SSID
        string "Default WiFi SSID"
        default "myssid"
        help
            Used when NVS holds no credentials yet. `sta <ssid> <pass>`
            overwrites what is stored in NVS.

    config APP_WIFI_PASSWORD
        string "Default WiFi password"
        default "mypassword"

    choice APP_CONTROL
        prompt "Control"
        default APP_CONTROL_CLI
        help
            Where settings come from. Either way the example adopts whatever
            link the coprocessor already holds before configuring anything.

        config APP_CONTROL_CLI
            bool "Console"
            help
                Nothing is applied at boot unless credentials were stored by a
                previous `sta` command. Drive everything from the prompt.

        config APP_CONTROL_KCONFIG
            bool "Kconfig"
            help
                Apply the settings below at boot.
    endchoice

    choice APP_WIFI_PS_MODE
        prompt "Wi-Fi power save mode"
        default APP_WIFI_PS_MIN_MODEM
        help
            Mirrors IDF's examples/wifi/power_save so measurements here are
            comparable with it.

            minimum modem: wake every DTIM to receive the beacon. Broadcast data
            is not lost, but DTIM is chosen by the AP so the saving is bounded.
            maximum modem: wake only every listen interval. Saves more, and is
            the only mode in which the listen interval below applies, but
            broadcast frames may be missed.

        config APP_WIFI_PS_NONE
            bool "none"
        config APP_WIFI_PS_MIN_MODEM
            bool "minimum modem"
        config APP_WIFI_PS_MAX_MODEM
            bool "maximum modem"
    endchoice

    config APP_WIFI_LISTEN_INTERVAL
        int "STA listen interval (beacons)"
        default 3
        help
            Beacons the radio may sleep through. Only honoured under
            WIFI_PS_MAX_MODEM. Default 3 matches
            CONFIG_EXAMPLE_WIFI_LISTEN_INTERVAL in IDF's wifi/power_save
            example; it still goes out in the association request in every mode.

    config APP_WIFI_MAX_RETRY
        int "Reconnect attempts"
        default 5

    config APP_PS_NVS_STATS
        bool "Count deep-sleep wakes in NVS"
        default n
        help
            Keep boot/wake counters and the last wake cause in NVS, and print
            them once the console is up.

            On a USB-serial-JTAG console the lines printed either side of a deep
            sleep are lost: output is buffered and sleep powers USB down before
            it drains. Counters in NVS survive the sleep, so they show that the
            host really slept and woke, and how many times.

            Example-level only; nothing in the hosted libraries is involved.
            One NVS commit per boot when enabled.

endmenu
